A||||3||FiXXXerX||How difficult is it to pull of the TB on a 4 cyl.?||||1||
Z||000000||FiXXXerX||12-28-2001||12:31 PM||||I need to know how difficult its gonna be for me to pull of the TBI unit off of an '84 4 cyl Fiero. How much ****  do I need to worry about, and about how long should it take. I gota Haynes manual but its at home. Need some help, supposed to go out to the Junkyard and pull it in a bit here.<P>Adam<P>------------------<BR>-= If the Front wheels don't leave the ground, its still broken =-||||reg||1
Z||000001||FiXXXerX||12-28-2001||12:55 PM||||Oh yeah, also, will an '84 TBI work on an '86? Both are 4 cyl. cars.<P>Adam<P>------------------<BR>-= If the Front wheels don't leave the ground, its still broken =-||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||12-28-2001||01:09 PM||||It's a 5 min. job.  Unplug the TPS and IAC wires, throttle linkage, and fuel lines then remove the three bolts that hold it to the manifold and you are done.  I think 86 and above use a different throttle body.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||12-28-2001||02:38 PM||||The 86 is the same as the 84.  The different ones were used starting with the 87 models that had the distributerless ignition.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
